GSP395 – Create and Manage AlloyDB Instances: Challenge Lab
Paste each block into Cloud Shell. Use the copy button.

1. Setup
bash
export REGION=us-east1   # change to the GCP Region on your lab page
export PROJECT_ID=$(gcloud config get-value project)
export VM_ZONE=$(gcloud compute instances list --filter="name=alloydb-client" --format="value(zone.basename())")
gcloud services enable alloydb.googleapis.com

2. Cluster and instance (10–15 min)
bash
gcloud beta alloydb clusters create lab-cluster --password=Change3Me --network=peering-network --region=$REGION --project=$PROJECT_ID
gcloud beta alloydb instances create lab-instance --instance-type=PRIMARY --cpu-count=2 --region=$REGION --cluster=lab-cluster --project=$PROJECT_ID
export ALLOYDB=$(gcloud beta alloydb instances describe lab-instance --cluster=lab-cluster --region=$REGION --format="value(ipAddress)")
echo $ALLOYDB
Check my progress: Create a cluster and instance

3. Tables and data
